{"content":[{"c":["BETHER*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Hebrew word occurring in the phrase “upon rugged mountains” and regarded as a proper name in the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," (“mountains of Bether,” ",{"href":"?bref=Song.2.17","r":"Song.2.17","rawR":"Song.2.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.2.17","value":"Song.2.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Sg 2:17"},"). Occurrence of the phrase “mountains of spices” in an almost identical verse (",{"href":"?bref=Song.8.14","r":"Song.8.14","rawR":"Song.8.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.8.14","value":"Song.8.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"8:14"},") suggests “spices” or a particular spice (such as cinnamon) as an appropriate translation of ",{"c":["bether"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},{"c":["."],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," Bether also occurs as the name of the city Beth-anoth in the hill country of Judah in ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.59","r":"Josh.15.59","rawR":"Josh.15.59","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.59","value":"Josh.15.59"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 15:59"}," (but only in the Septuagint). In ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.59","r":"1Chr.6.59","rawR":"1Chr.6.59","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.59","value":"1Chr.6.59"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 6:59"}," the Septuagint reads “Bether” instead of “Beth-shemesh.” Some scholars identify this Bether with Khir-bet el-Jehudiyeh, southwest of Bittir, which may preserve the ancient name. It is unlikely that Bether is related to the phrase “mountains of Bether.”"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In ",{"c":["AD"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," 135, Bether became the site of the last Jewish stronghold against the Romans in the Second Revolt (",{"c":["AD"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," 132–135). There Simon Bar-Kochba, the designated “messiah,” and the Jewish forces were massacred."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bether","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Sg 2:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.2.17","rawQueryValue":"Song.2.17","sourceRefExact":"Song.2.17"},{"anchorText":"8:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.8.14","rawQueryValue":"Song.8.14","sourceRefExact":"Song.8.14"},{"anchorText":"Joshua 15:59","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.59","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.59","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.59"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 6:59","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.59","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.59","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.59"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5e565575ec19d093f1fa7484c584abcb77d2c4017ee81969a4a335f392100c97","sourceItemName":"Bether","sourceItemOrder":246,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bether","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bether*","title":"Bether*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}